  "pokedexEntries": [
    {
      "game": "Red",
      "text": "When several of these POKéMON gather, their electricity could build and cause lightning storms."
    },
    {
      "game": "Yellow",
      "text": "It keeps its tail raised to monitor its surroundings. If you yank its tail, it will try to bite you."
    },
    {
      "game": "Gold",
      "text": "This intelligent POKéMON roasts hard BERRIES with electricity to make them tender enough to eat."
    },
    {
      "game": "Silver",
      "text": "It raises its tail to check its sur roundings. The tail is sometimes struck by light ning in this pose."
    },
    {
      "game": "Crystal",
      "text": "When it is anger ed, it immediately discharges the energy stored in the pouches in its cheeks."
    },
    {
      "game": "Ruby",
      "text": "Whenever PIKACHU comes across something new, it blasts it with a jolt of electricity. If you come across a blackened berry, it’s evidence that this POKéMON mistook the intensity of its charge."
    },
    {
      "game": "Sapphire",
      "text": "This POKéMON has electricity-storing pouches on its cheeks. These appear to become electrically charged during the night while PIKACHU sleeps. It occasionally discharges electricity when it is dozy after waking up."
    },
    {
      "game": "Emerald",
      "text": "It stores electricity in the electric sacs on its cheeks. When it releases pent-up energy in a burst, the electric power is equal to a lightning bolt."
    },
    {
      "game": "Firered",
      "text": "It has small electric sacs on both its cheeks. If threatened, it looses electric charges from the sacs."
    },
    {
      "game": "Leafgreen",
      "text": "When several of these POKéMON gather, their electricity can build and cause lightning storms."
    },
    {
      "game": "Diamond",
      "text": "It lives in forests with others. It stores electricity in the pouches on its cheeks."
    },
    {
      "game": "Pearl",
      "text": "If it looses crackling power from the electric pouches on its cheeks, it is being wary."
    },
    {
      "game": "Platinum",
      "text": "It occasionally uses an electric shock to recharge a fellow PIKACHU that is in a weakened state."
    },
    {
      "game": "Soulsilver",
      "text": "It raises its tail to check its surroundings. The tail is sometimes struck by lightning in this pose."
    },
    {
      "game": "Sun",
      "text": "A plan was recently announced to gather many Pikachu and make an electric power plant."
    },
    {
      "game": "Moon",
      "text": "It’s in its nature to store electricity. It feels stressed now and then if it’s unable to fully discharge the electricity."
    },
    {
      "game": "Ultra Sun",
      "text": "Its nature is to store up electricity. Forests where nests of Pikachu live are dangerous, since the trees are so often struck by lightning."
    },
    {
      "game": "Ultra Moon",
      "text": "While sleeping, it generates electricity in the sacs in its cheeks. If it’s not getting enough sleep, it will be able to use only weak electricity."
    },
    {
      "game": "Lets Go Pikachu",
      "text": "This forest-dwelling Pokémon stores electricity in its cheeks, so you’ll feel a tingly shock if you touch it."
    },
    {
      "game": "Sword",
      "text": "Pikachu that can generate powerful electricity have cheek sacs that are extra soft and super stretchy."
    },
    {
      "game": "Shield",
      "text": "When Pikachu meet, they’ll touch their tails together and exchange electricity through them as a form of greeting."
    },
    {
      "game": "Legends Arceus",
      "text": "Possesses cheek sacs in which it stores electricity. This clever forest-dweller roasts tough berries with an electric shock before consuming them."
    }
  ],
